Sure! Below is a simple example of an **interactive rotating card** using only HTML and CSS.  
When you hover over the card, it will smoothly rotate around its center.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
/* Basic reset */
* { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }

/* Center the card on the page */
body {
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    height:100vh;
    background:#f0f0f0;
}

/* Card container */
.card {
    width:260px;
    height:360px;
    perspective:800px;          /* Gives depth to the 3D effect */
    cursor:pointer;
}

/* Card inner wrapper (the part that actually rotates) */
.card-inner {
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    position:relative;
    transition:transform 0.6s ease;   /* Smooth rotation */
    transform-style:preserve-3d;      /* Keep children in 3D space */
}

/* Hover effect – rotate 180° around Y axis */
.card:hover .card-inner {
    transform:rotateY(180deg);
}

/* Front & back faces */
.card-face {
    position:absolute;
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    backface-visibility:hidden;       /* Hide backside when rotated */
    border-radius:12px;
    overflow:hidden;
    box-shadow:0 4px 10px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
}

/* Front face styling */
.card-front {
    background:#fff;
    display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;
    align-items:center;
    justify-content:center;
    padding:20px;
    text-align:center;
}

.card-front img {
    max-width:80%;
    border-radius:8px;
    margin-bottom:15px;
}

.card-front h3 {
    font-size:1.5rem;
    color:#333;
    margin-bottom:10px;
}

.card-front p {
    font-size:1rem;
    color:#666;
}

/* Back face styling */
.card-back {
    background:#fafafa;
    transform:rotateY(180deg);        /* Position back side behind front */
    display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;
    align-items:center;
    justify-content:center;
    padding:20px;
    text-align:center;
}

.card-back h3 {
    font-size:1.5rem;
    color:#222;
    margin-bottom:10px;
}

.card-back p {
    font-size:1rem;
    color:#555;
}
</style>
</head>

<body>
<div class="card">
    <div class="card-inner">
        <!-- Front Face -->
        <div class="card-face card-front">
            <img src="https://picsum.photos/200/150" alt="Sample Image">
            <h3>Tytuł karty</h3>
            <p>To jest przykładowy opis frontu karty.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Back Face -->
        <div class="card-face card-back">
            <h3>Back Side</h3>
            <p>Tu znajduje się dodatkowa treść, która pojawia się po obróceniu karty.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Element | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `.card` | Wrapper with `perspective` to give depth. |
| `.card-inner` | Rotates on hover (`transform: rotateY(180deg)`), with smooth transition. |
| `.card-face` | Both front and back faces share common styles. |
| `backface-visibility: hidden` | Hides the backside when not visible. |
| `transform: rotateY(180deg)` on `.card-back` | Positions the back face behind the front. |

Feel free to replace the image URL, text, or colors to match your design. Enjoy creating interactive cards!
